The function only copies its members, and I don't see a meaningful safe speedup here. The real cost is in `FieldBase`'s copy constructor, which this function can't change. The rewrite below is behavior-identical: it makes the base-class copy explicit and keeps the members in their declared order. I don't expect it to measurably change decode time.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(static_cast<const FieldBase&>(field))
    , profile(field.profile)
    , profileIndex(field.profileIndex)
    , type(field.type)
    , isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
}
```